<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrei Rublev</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1360–c. 1428</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrei Rublev was the most celebrated Russian icon painter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, a monk associated with the Trinity Monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sergius-of-radonezh">Sergius of Radonezh</a> and the Andronikov Monastery in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>. He worked with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theophanes-the-greek">Theophanes the Greek</a> on the Annunciation Cathedral in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow-kremlin">Moscow Kremlin</a> and painted frescoes in the Dormition Cathedral at Vladimir in 1408. His icon of the Trinity, painted in the early fifteenth century, is regarded as the summit of Russian religious art.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andrei-rublev.jpg" alt="Andrei Rublev" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Podgorica,_cattedrale_della_resurrezione_di_cristo,_interno_0_Andrej_Rublev.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
